---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="NIELIT O Level Syllabus, Notes & Study Material (R5.1 Aligned) | Skilldotpy"
  description="Master NIELIT O Level examination with full syllabus breakdown for M1-R5.1, M2-R5.1, M3-R5.1, and M4-R5.1. Free chapter notes, 60:40 formula guide, practical test questions and PDF downloads."
  keywords={[
    "NIELIT O Level syllabus R5.1 pdf",
    "O Level M1-R5 IT Tools notes",
    "O Level M2-R5 Web Design syllabus",
    "O Level M3-R5 Python practical syllabus",
    "O Level M4-R5 IoT notes Hindi",
    "O Level 60:40 passing marks calculation",
    "Skilldotpy O Level"
  ]}
  type="course"
>
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10">
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-10 text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 text-xs font-bold rounded-full inline-block mb-3">
        DOEACC / NIELIT NSQF Level 4
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-3">
        NIELIT O Level (IT) Course Complete Guide
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
        Everything you need to qualify all 4 modules (M1-R5.1, M2-R5.1, M3-R5.1, M4-R5.1), practical exams (PR1-PR4), and project work (PJ1-R5.1) with Grade S/A.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Exam Pattern & Passing Formula (Critical for Google ranking & student search intent) -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>📊</span> NIELIT O Level Examination Pattern & 60:40 Rule
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 text-sm">
        <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 block mb-1">1. Theory Exam (100 MCQs)</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            100 Objective Questions on OMR/Online CBT. 2 Hours duration. <strong>No negative marking</strong>. Min 33% required. Contributes <strong>60% weightage</strong> to final grade.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <span class="font-bold text-slate-900 block mb-1">2. Practical Exam (100 Marks)</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            80 Marks Lab Demonstration + 20 Marks Viva Voce. 3 Hours. Min 33% required. Contributes <strong>40% weightage</strong> to final module result.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-xl border border-blue-200">
          <span class="font-bold text-blue-900 block mb-1">3. Overall Passing Criteria</span>
          <p class="text-xs text-blue-800 leading-relaxed">
            Must score at least <strong>50% in the weighted combined score</strong>: <br/>
            <code>Score = (Theory Marks × 0.60) + (Practical Marks × 0.40)</code>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 4 Module Detail Sections -->
    <div class="space-y-8">
      <!-- M1-R5.1 -->
      <section id="m1" class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 text-xs font-bold rounded-full">Module 1 (M1-R5.1)</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-medium">Credits: 4 | Total Hours: 120</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          Information Technology Tools and Network Basics
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Covers computer hardware, GUI operating system (Linux/Windows), LibreOffice Suite (Writer, Calc, Impress), Networking concepts, Internet, Email, Digital Financial Services, and Cyber Security.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="/notes/m1-r5-ch1-introduction-to-computer" class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-blue-50 text-blue-700 text-xs font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-100 transition">
            Read Chapter 1 Notes →
          </a>
          <a href="/mock-test" class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 text-xs font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-slate-200 transition">
            Take M1 Mock Test
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- M2-R5.1 -->
      <section id="m2" class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-800 text-xs font-bold rounded-full">Module 2 (M2-R5.1)</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-medium">Credits: 4 | Total Hours: 120</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          Web Designing & Publishing
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Master HTML5 semantic tags, CSS3 flexbox/grid styling, W3.CSS responsive framework, client-side JavaScript DOM manipulation, Angular JS basics, and Photo Editing (GIMP/Photoshop).
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="/mock-test" class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700 text-xs font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-emerald-100 transition">
            Take M2 Mock Test →
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- M3-R5.1 -->
      <section id="m3" class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-amber-100 text-amber-800 text-xs font-bold rounded-full">Module 3 (M3-R5.1)</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-medium">Credits: 5 | Total Hours: 150</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          Programming and Problem Solving through Python
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          Algorithms, flowcharts, Python data types (lists, tuples, dicts, sets), conditional execution, loops, function definitions, recursion, file operations, and NumPy array operations.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="/notes/m3-r5-ch1-python-programming-basics" class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-amber-50 text-amber-700 text-xs font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-amber-100 transition">
            Read Python Chapter 1 Notes →
          </a>
          <a href="/mock-test" class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-slate-100 text-slate-700 text-xs font-semibold rounded-lg hover:bg-slate-200 transition">
            Take Python Mock Test
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- M4-R5.1 -->
      <section id="m4" class="bg-white border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-4">
          <span class="px-3 py-1 bg-purple-100 text-purple-800 text-xs font-bold rounded-full">Module 4 (M4-R5.1)</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-medium">Credits: 4 | Total Hours: 120</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">
          Internet of Things and its Applications (IoT)
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-600 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          IoT ecosystem, hardware platforms (Arduino UNO, Raspberry Pi), sensors, actuators, communication protocols (MQTT, CoAP), microcontrollers, building IoT applications, and soft skills.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="/mock-test" class="px-3 py-1.5 bg-purple-50 text-purple-700 text-xs font-bold rounded-lg hover:bg-purple-100 transition">
            Take IoT Mock Test →
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
